## What are cookies?

Cookies are small files that a website stores on your device. Similar technology, like your browser's **local storage**, works in a similar way. The law (the Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations, or PECR) says websites must tell you about these and, in most cases, ask for your permission first.

## Why there is no cookie banner

Since changes made by the **Data (Use and Access) Act 2025**, websites do not need your consent for storage that is **strictly necessary** for a service you ask for, or for some **low-risk statistics**, as long as you are told about them and can easily say no.

We only use technology that falls into these groups, so we do not need a banner. We do **not** use:

- advertising cookies
- cookies that track you across other websites
- social media tracking pixels
- tools that record your screen or mouse movements

## What we do use

| Name | Type | What it does | How long it lasts |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| juniper-checker-pip, juniper-checker-aa, juniper-checker-dla | Local storage | Only created if **you press "Save my answers on this device"** in a self-check. Keeps your answers on your device so you can come back to them. Never sent to us. | Until you press "Start again" or clear your browser data |
| jh-analytics-optout | Local storage | Only created if **you switch statistics off** below. Remembers your choice. | Until you switch statistics back on or clear your browser data |
| __cf_bm, cf_clearance | Cookie (set by Cloudflare) | Security cookies that Cloudflare may set to tell people apart from harmful bots. They do not track you. | Up to 30 minutes (__cf_bm) or up to a year (cf_clearance) |

These are all **strictly necessary** or are only created because **you asked for them**, so they do not need consent.

## Visitor statistics

We use **Cloudflare Web Analytics** to count visits and see how fast our pages load. It **does not set cookies** or use local storage, does not collect your IP address for tracking, and does not follow you to other websites. We only see totals.

We also do not load it if your browser sends a **Global Privacy Control** or **Do Not Track** signal.

### Switch off statistics

{% analyticsOptOut /%}

## Other websites

Our pages contain links to other websites, including GOV.UK, the NHS, charities and, where clearly labelled, shops through affiliate links. **We do not place cookies for them on our site.** If you visit those websites, they may use their own cookies, and their own cookie policies apply.

## The Keystatic editor

The page at /keystatic is only used by the people who edit this website. It uses cookies to keep editors signed in. Visitors to our website never see or use it.

## How to control cookies in your browser

You can block or delete cookies and stored data in your browser settings. Blocking our storage will not stop our website working, but you will not be able to save self-check answers.

- [Google Chrome](https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647)
- [Safari on iPhone and iPad](https://support.apple.com/en-gb/105082)
- [Mozilla Firefox](https://support.mozilla.org/en-US/kb/clear-cookies-and-site-data-firefox)
- [Microsoft Edge](https://support.microsoft.com/en-gb/microsoft-edge/delete-cookies-in-microsoft-edge-63947406-40ac-c3b8-57b9-2a946a29ae09)

## Changes and questions

If we ever want to use cookies that need your consent, we will update this policy and ask you first. If you have any questions, email hello@juniperhealth.app. See also our [privacy policy](/privacy-policy/).
